<title>NEW ZEALAND: CentralPower to return NZ$27.5 mln to s/holders.</title>
<headline>CentralPower to return NZ$27.5 mln to s/holders.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>CentralPower Ltd said on Thursday it had received High Court approval to return NZ$27.5 million of capital to its shareholders.</p>
<p>Under the Companies Act, the capital repayment needed High Court approval before the payment could be made.</p>
<p>The repayment amount will be based on the number of shares held by a shareholder at 5 p.m. on October 25. The repayment involves the cancellation of one share in five held by every shareholder, and a payment of NZ$2.50 per cancelled share.  </p>
<p>Infrastructure and Utilities NZ Ltd (Infratil) owns 21 percent of CentralPower, which is based in the Manawatu region of the North Island.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
